/E (A psychological and emotional toll of school exclusion and early marriage is profound, and that it begins well before any marriage takes place. Loss of education removes not only a pathway to the future but also a daily source of structure, recognition, and hope. Several participants described anxiety, fear, shame, sadness, and a sense that their lives had been paused or emptied of meaning once sixth finding is that the their education ended.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
