/E (Her words capture how the foreclosure of education is experienced not merely as a lost opportunity but as a grief. These testimonies underscore that the consequences of school exclusion are psychological and emotional as well as physical, legal, and material, and that mental-health support belongs alongside protection and education in any adequate response. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
