/E (Across themselves identified what would make the greatest difference to their lives. Their priorities centred on the restoration of access to education, whether through the reopening of the interviews, the girls schools community-based or safe alternative learning, and on protection from forced and early marriage, and on recognition of their own voice in decisions about their futures. They expressed a continuing desire to learn and a determination that the next generation should not face the same closure of opportunity. These priorities are reflected directly in the recommendations that follow.  )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [9]
>>
