/Title (Aexclusion systems that might otherwise help prevent child marriage. Teachers, school administrators, and education staff can serve as early warning points when girls face distress, pressure, or risk of abuse. Once girls are removed fourth finding is that school protective iundermines from school, those institutional contact points disappear. UNICEF has emphasized that community-based learning can help mitigate some harm, but formal exclusion on a national scale leaves large numbers of girls outside regular systems of visibility and support.31)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1649 0 R
/Next 1666 0 R
>>
endobj
1658 0 obj
<<
