/Title (Aggregating all marriages before age 18 into a single measure \(Figure 2\) underscores both the national scale and the wide provincial variation. The national survey-weighted estimate is a near-even split, with about 49% of young women married as children and 51% as adults. Prevalence is lowest in provinces such as Paktya \(22.6%\), Logar \(23.1%\), and Parwan \(32.4%\), and highest in Helmand \(64.1%\), Herat \(61.5%\), and Faryab \(58.7%\). This range of more than forty percentage points reflects the close link between child marriage and local conditions of poverty, displacement, and access to schooling.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1655 0 R
/Next 1667 0 R
>>
endobj
