/Title (The central finding of this report is that the exclusion of girls from school functions as a direct driver of child marriage risk. Lack of access to education is one of the major drivers of child marriage in Afghanistan.28 Schooling often provides girls with structure, social recognition, and a concrete reason to postpone marriage. It also supports future aspirations and gives families a)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1671 0 R
/Next 1677 0 R
>>
endobj
1677 0 obj
<<
/Title (legitimate engagement basis for delaying marriage arrangements. When that pathway is removed, marriage may be reframed as the natural or only remaining option. Interview evidence strongly supports this described moment conclusion. Several girls the marriage-related discussions became more frequent or closure as when)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1671 0 R
/Prev 1676 0 R
>>
endobj
